# Recipe for script/combat/bard-necro-enhanced.razor. Build it with: node util/build-scripts.mjs
# Every setting of this loop: node util/build-scripts.mjs --settings recipe/bard-necro-enhanced-recipe.razor
# @ output script/combat/bard-necro-enhanced.razor


# ========================================================================================
# @ header
# ========================================================================================

# Bard Necro Enhanced: sustain, bard control, necro burst, opener and damage rotation.
# Design, cooldown model and every barding number: content/public/templates/bard-necro.md
# (design in part 5, mechanics in part 2).
# Needs: Discordance, Peacemaking and Provocation trained (the song round robin parks on a
# missing one), an instrument in the backpack, a necromancer book, and reagents.
# Provo candidates: V (closest monster), or Shift+Space (Set Last Target, Beneficial),
# then [ provo, set ]. Q changes only the bard target. Register in warmode until native
# cursor overlap is checked in-game (content/public/questions/open-items.md part 17).
# The hotbar's own Auto-Renew must be OFF for every ability this loop drives: it spends
# the same symbols, cheapest first.
# cooldowns.xml carries every bar this loop reads: music, song, disco, peace/provo, magic
# arrow, harm, fireball, lightning, heal pot, reflect and walk. The names are lowercase
# and the glossary is content/public/scripting/overheads.md.
# A fight is a hostile inside target_range. In a fight: Provocation of the enemies you
# picked onto each other, Discordance, Peacemaking, the necro burst, the opener, the proc
# core, the filler and Poison Strike. On the walk: the self buffs, Spell Siphon, the bard
# song and Vampiric Embrace. Mushrooms are eaten in either, and Create Food makes more on
# the walk.
# The two summons are kept out in either: Vengeful Spirit, then the missing one. Under 65
# mana Wither pays part of the cast, and the other necro abilities leave it the symbols.
# With no enemy near, a summon out ten minutes is released by name and cast again.
# Warmode is the player's manual window: our casts, the bard skills, the self buffs,
# Create Food, the summons, Corpse Skin and Evil Omen stand down. Cures, heals, potions,
# the mushroom and Blood Oath keep running.
# Herding is off: the slot went to Resisting Spells on 2026-09-27. Add tamer/herding to the
# blocks when it comes back.


# ========================================================================================
# @ blocks
#
#   One box per block, in the order the blocks run, base first. The builder writes the box.
#   Yours are the "> " lines in it (a note on the block, or under a setting the reason for
#   its value) and the @setvar! lines under it. Write a new @setvar! line under any box, its
#   reason as a "#" line right above it: the builder moves both to the box it belongs to.
# ========================================================================================

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ use base
#
#   The frame of every loop and routine. Every recipe lists it first.
#
#   warmode_is_manual (default 0)
#      Whose warmode it is.
#        0  ours: our casts ignore it
#        1  the player's manual control window: our casts and the food stand down while it
#           is on. Potions and bandages still go out
#      Read by recovery/cure, recovery/heal, recovery/light-heal, buff/food,
#         necro/resummon, buff/spells.
#      > The player casts by hand in warmode: our casts, buffs and food stand down then.
#
#   recover_in_warmode (default 0)
#      With warmode_is_manual 1, what the recovery casts (cure, heal, light Heal) do in
#      warmode.
#        0  stand down with the rest
#        1  keep going, so only the other casts wait for the player
#      Read by recovery/cure, recovery/heal, recovery/light-heal.
#      > What keeps the character alive keeps running in warmode.
#
#   use_bandages (default 1)
#      1 uses bandages. At 0 recovery/light-heal stands in.
#      Read by recovery/light-heal.
#      > No bandages in this loop: the light Heal agent stands in for them.
#
#   settle_first (default 0)
#      What a pass does first.
#        0  reads the state at once. Potions still go out while a spell is casting
#        1  waits for the item queue and any cast to finish, then wait__cast_cursor more
#           after a cast, for its cursor to be answered
#      > Anything already in flight finishes before the pass reads state.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@setvar! config__warmode_is_manual 1
@setvar! config__recover_in_warmode 1
@setvar! config__use_bandages 0
@setvar! config__settle_first 1

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ use bard/provo-picks
#
#   Registers changed lastbeneficial enemies as Provocation candidates, before our casts.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ========================================================================================
# @ when paralyzed or poisoned or diffhits > 0
# ========================================================================================

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ use recovery/cure
#
#   The trapped pouch while paralyzed, else a cure potion or the Smart Heal/Cure agent.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ use recovery/heal
#
#   Heal potion at heal_hits, else Greater Heal at emergency_hits.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ use recovery/light-heal
#
#   The light Heal agent: the bandage stand-in, or beside them with use_light_heal 1.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ========================================================================================
# @ end
# ========================================================================================

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ use fight/target
#
#   Remembers the picked enemy and sets var__fighting while it is in reach.
#
#   acquire_range (default 12)
#      How far the enemy you pick is taken up from, and kept while it stays. The pets
#      often open on a mob past target_range, and a song or self cast would otherwise
#      move lastharmful off it before it comes in reach.
#      Also read by bard/provo-picks, bard/provo, bard/disco, bard/peace, magery/rotation,
#         necro/poison-strike, necro/vampiric-embrace.
#      > The whole screen: the pets often open on a mob well past target_range.
#
#   target_range (default 12)
#      How far the remembered enemy may be and still count as a fight (var__fighting 1).
#      Not above acquire_range.
#      Also read by bard/provo, bard/disco, bard/peace, magery/rotation,
#         necro/poison-strike.
#      > The bard and spell stages engage inside this range.
#
#   target_grace (default 1200)
#      How long, in ms, a remembered enemy that left acquire_range is kept.
#      > A target that left the screen is dropped half a second later.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@setvar! config__acquire_range 18
@setvar! config__target_range 10
@setvar! config__target_grace 500

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ use magery/reagents
#
#   Reagent flags for the Magery casts, the mana per circle and the shared cast settings.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ use necro/symbols
#
#   Keeps the necro hotbar open and reads its Unholy Symbol count into a list.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ========================================================================================
# @ every interval__housekeeping
# ========================================================================================

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ use bard/instrument
#
#   Finds the instrument before the loop and keeps track of it while the loop runs.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ use recovery/refresh
#
#   Total Refresh at or below refresh_stam.
#
#   refresh_stam (default 15)
#      Current stamina at or below this drinks a Refresh.
#      > Only a nearly empty stamina bar is worth a Refresh here.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@setvar! config__refresh_stam 4

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ use buff/food
#
#   Eats from a tray while Food Satisfaction is missing, looked at once a minute.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ use necro/summon-names
#
#   Names each fresh summon after its kind: leech, mumi, vampa, wichy and so on.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ use pack/gold-drop
#
#   Drops gold at your feet while over max weight, one drop per pass.
#
#   gold_drop_amount (default 2000)
#      Gold dropped per pass while over max weight. Gold is cheaper than the leather.
#      > Weight only changes on a pickup: one smaller lift per housekeeping tick.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@setvar! config__gold_drop_amount 1000

# ========================================================================================
# @ end
# ========================================================================================

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ use buff/potions
#
#   Strength and Agility by stat value, Magic Resist by its icon, while fighting.
#
#   dex_potion (default 100)
#      DEX with the Greater Agility potion on: your base plus 20. Below it the potion is
#      drunk, and 0 turns it off. Bless and the Agility spell show the same icon, as for
#      STR.
#      > This template is DEX 25: base plus 20 with the Greater Agility potion.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@setvar! config__dex_potion 45

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ use buff/mushroom
#
#   Eats a Magic Mushroom at low mana, and makes more with Create Food at high mana.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ use necro/resummon
#
#   Keeps two undead summons out through Vengeful Spirit, and replaces worn ones.
#
#   summon_first (default 1)
#      The summon that goes out first, by the spell cast under Vengeful Spirit. When the
#      two differ, this one is looked for by its body to tell which is missing, so it
#      cannot be 4, whose body is not known yet. Play warns when it is.
#        1  Fire Elemental, a lich
#        2  Water Elemental, a rag witch
#        3  Earth Elemental, an ancient mummy
#        4  Air Elemental, a skeletal fiend
#        5  Summon Daemon, a vampire thrall
#      > The user's pair, 2026-10-18. The rag witch tanks, so it goes first.
#
#   summon_second (default 1)
#      The other summon, numbered as config__summon_first. The same number as the first
#      keeps two of a kind.
#      > The ancient mummy, the other half of the user's pair.
#
#   summon_refresh (default 0)
#      How long, in ms, a summon stays out before it is released and cast again, while
#      no enemy is remembered. 0 turns it off. A skeletal fiend has no name to release it
#      by, so it stays. A release waits for config__summon_mana and is refilled on the
#      same pass, so Wither is never spent on one.
#      > Ten minutes leaves about 55% of max health: 1% every 10 seconds, compounding.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@setvar! config__summon_first 2
@setvar! config__summon_second 3
@setvar! config__summon_refresh 600000

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ use bard/provo
#
#   Provokes registered candidates in order, two at a time, including the bard target.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ========================================================================================
# @ when var__fighting = 1
# ========================================================================================

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ use bard/disco
#
#   Discordance once per target, read off its label, then left alone for 30 seconds.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ use bard/peace
#
#   Peacemaking kept up on the target, waiting out a pacify or a barding break.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ use necro/burst
#
#   Blood Oath, Corpse Skin and Evil Omen in value order, one per pass.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ use magery/rotation
#
#   The Grimoire rotation: Mana Drain and Curse, the four proc spells, then Energy Bolt.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ use necro/poison-strike
#
#   Poison Strike once the proc core is spent, while Corpse Skin is up.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ========================================================================================
# @ otherwise
# ========================================================================================

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ use buff/spells
#
#   Reactive Armor, then Magic Reflection, whenever one is missing.
#
#   use_spell_siphon (default 0)
#      1 keeps the Spell Siphon buff up with a Magic Arrow on yourself, never while Magic
#      Reflection is up, since the arrow would only burn the reflection. Warmode off.
#      > The walk keeps Spell Siphon up with a Magic Arrow on self.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@setvar! config__use_spell_siphon 1

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ use bard/song
#
#   One bard song per walk pass with no enemy remembered, Discordance, Peacemaking and
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ use necro/vampiric-embrace
#
#   Vampiric Embrace from a walk surplus of Unholy Symbols, near a corpse.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ========================================================================================
# @ end
# ========================================================================================


# ========================================================================================
# @ setup
# ========================================================================================

# loot/recycle runs the hotkey named in this list when it finishes or gives up. A list, because
# a variable cannot hold a word (content/public/scripting/razor.md part 3). It lasts until the client closes.
if not listexists 'list__resume_script'
    createlist 'list__resume_script'
endif

clearlist 'list__resume_script'
pushlist 'list__resume_script' 'Play Script: combat\bard-necro-enhanced'

if config__chatty = 1
    overhead "[ bard necro, on ]" 290
endif
